{
  "change_type": "major",
  "title": "GatedRubric-GRPO: Continuous Hierarchical Gating with Decoupled Normalization for Non-Verifiable Multimodal Scientific Reasoning",
  "core_problem": "Reinforcement learning with structured rewards has advanced rapidly across three converging axes: (1) gated/hierarchical rewards for verifiable multimodal tasks (PaLMR, PEARL, CogFlow use binary visual gates; VGPO uses a binary Visual Gate for attention compensation), (2) rubric-based RL for non-verifiable tasks (RaR [ICLR 2026] uses rubric rewards with GRPO for medicine/science; DRO uses binary rubric-gates as feasibility constraints; Training AI Co-Scientists applies rubric RL to scientific plan generation), and (3) perception-aware VLM training (VPPO, PAPO, From Seeing to Thinking [ICML 2026] demonstrate perception-first training is critical; Bad Seeing or Bad Thinking [ICML 2026] introduces MoCA for perception-reasoning credit assignment; Perceval integrates claim-level perception verification into RL training via token-level advantage modulation). However, ALL existing gating mechanisms in RL training employ BINARY or DISCRETE constraint mechanisms: hard accept/reject, pass/fail, or threshold-based Lagrangian penalties. Furthermore, GDPO (ICML 2026) proves that naive GRPO normalization of multi-reward aggregation causes distinct reward combinations to collapse into identical advantage values. The problem is especially acute for non-verifiable scientific visual reasoning where both visual grounding quality and reasoning quality are INHERENTLY CONTINUOUS and GRADED.",
  "description": "We propose GatedRubric-GRPO, a framework that introduces CONTINUOUS hierarchical gating with DECOUPLED NORMALIZATION for non-verifiable multimodal scientific reasoning. The work makes three contributions: (1) An original analytical result (Proposition 1: Degenerate Group Elimination) proving that continuous sigmoid gating eliminates gate-induced degenerate GRPO groups and achieves strictly higher expected within-group gate variance at optimal temperature. (2) A novel reward architecture combining continuous sigmoid gates with GDPO-style decoupled per-tier normalization preventing multi-reward advantage collapse. Three epistemically dependent tiers are combined as R = w1*R1 + w2*g1(R1)*R2 + w3*g1(R1)*g2(R2)*R3. (3) A comprehensive 11-condition ablation suite including FGRPO-style Lagrangian constraints, GDPO vs AP-GRPO normalization, and binary gating variants. Training on MMSci (10K), SciGraphQA, and SciCritique-5K (new benchmark)."
}
